{
 "product_id": "p-bpd-001",
 "items": [
  {
   "key": "must:mh_business",
   "kind": "must_have",
   "text": "Built for running a business, not a general life planner: every week page has Content to post and Follow up, every day page has Calls and emails and Orders to send, plus Year plan, Price check, Business routines and Money month pages."
  },
  {
   "key": "must:mh_calendar",
   "kind": "must_have",
   "text": "Full dated 2027 calendar: year, 12 months, 52 weeks and 365 day pages, every date, tab and trail linked, so it replaces a diary as well as the business templates."
  },
  {
   "key": "must:mh_apps",
   "kind": "must_have",
   "text": "One hyperlinked PDF that works in Goodnotes, Notability, Noteshelf, Samsung Notes, Xodo and Adobe Acrobat Reader; the listing names these apps and says no subscription is needed."
  },
  {
   "key": "must:mh_look",
   "kind": "must_have",
   "text": "Calm, uncluttered pages with clear hierarchy and plenty of writing room; two font families only, sharp vector text at any zoom."
  },
  {
   "key": "must:mh_easy",
   "kind": "must_have",
   "text": "Easy to start and the same layout every week: Start here page with four steps, Setup check, Contents with every section and month."
  },
  {
   "key": "must:mh_content",
   "kind": "must_have",
   "text": "Content planning built into the calendar (Launches and content on every month page, Content to post on every week page, Content ideas pages), because social media and content planners are a large share of what this market sells."
  },
  {
   "key": "fix:fx_not_useful",
   "kind": "fix",
   "text": "complaint:c_not_useful: Aimed at one clear buyer, the one-person business, with pages for what that buyer does every week: Money month (money in by source, money out by cost type, profit, orders, best seller), Price check (cost, fees, time, price, profit per product), Content to post and Follow up on every week page. The listing's first lines say who it is for and what it is not (not a business plan workbook, not a printable, not made to order), so buyers with other needs do not buy it."
  },
  {
   "key": "fix:fx_misleading",
   "kind": "fix",
   "text": "complaint:c_misleading: Listing copy states the exact page count and file size of the built file (r003), what each page type is and how many there are (53 week pages, 365 day pages, 12 Money months, and so on), that it is one landscape PDF, dated Oct 26, 2026 to Dec 2027, Monday start. No page is counted twice. Photo ph10 shows the Contents page so the buyer sees every section before buying."
  },
  {
   "key": "fix:fx_download",
   "kind": "fix",
   "text": "complaint:c_download: One PDF delivered as a direct Etsy download (no zip, no outside link, no sign-up). The listing's first FAQ line and step 1 of the Start here page say: download in a web browser, not the Etsy app, then open the PDF in a named app. File size is stated in the listing so buyers on slow connections know what to expect."
  },
  {
   "key": "fix:fx_basic",
   "kind": "fix",
   "text": "complaint:c_basic: Business depth on top of the calendar: Money month for each month (plus Nov and Dec 2026), a Year plan with quarter tick boxes, Price check, Business routines (daily, weekly, monthly, quarterly), a business habit tracker for every 2027 month, and content slots on month and week pages. Photos ph3 and ph5 show these pages close up."
  },
  {
   "key": "fix:fx_value",
   "kind": "fix",
   "text": "complaint:c_value: A complete working year, not a few templates: about 480 linked pages (exact count from the build in the listing) covering Oct 26, 2026 to Dec 31, 2027, with business pages that a spreadsheet does not give you in one place (week plan, content, follow ups and month money side by side). Every link is tested by the build (r001) so nothing in the price is broken."
  },
  {
   "key": "fix:fx_quality",
   "kind": "fix",
   "text": "complaint:c_quality: Vector PDF: all text and lines are drawn as vectors with embedded OFL fonts, so pages stay sharp at any zoom (no blurry raster pages). Pages are 1024 x 768 (iPad landscape) with every element inside the page margins, checked by the build's overflow check. Photo ph10 includes a zoomed crop of small text to show it is sharp. The listing says the pages are sized for a screen, not for letter or A4 paper."
  },
  {
   "key": "fix:fx_edit",
   "kind": "fix",
   "text": "complaint:c_edit: Start here step 3 says how to type: every line and table row is tall enough for the app's text box tool (Goodnotes, Notability, Xodo, Acrobat Reader), so keyboard users can type on any page; table rows are 30 px or more. The listing says plainly: write with a stylus or type with your app's text tool; there are no fill-in form fields and it is not a Word or Canva template."
  },
  {
   "key": "fix:fx_hard",
   "kind": "fix",
   "text": "complaint:c_hard: Two habits run the planner: the week page every Monday and the Money month at month end (the Start here tip says so). The Start here page gives four numbered steps; the Setup check confirms links before planning; the same week and day layout repeats all year so there is nothing new to learn after week one. Photo ph7 shows the Start here and Setup check pages."
  },
  {
   "key": "fix:fx_support",
   "kind": "fix",
   "text": "complaint:c_support: Help is printed in the file, so a buyer does not have to wait for a reply: the Setup check page lists the four fixes for links that do not jump, and the Start here page covers download, apps, writing and typing. The listing has the same answers as an FAQ. No reply-time promises anywhere (r007); the buyer is told they can send the shop an Etsy message."
  },
  {
   "key": "fix:fx_nav",
   "kind": "fix",
   "text": "complaint:c_nav: Every page has the top bar (Home, Year, Goals, Prices, Content, Notes, Money) and the month tabs on the right edge; calendar pages show a tappable Year / Month / Week trail; the Contents page has a card for every section and all months; the Start here page maps the top bar. No scrolling: every page is reachable in two taps from Contents (r001)."
  },
  {
   "key": "fix:fx_device",
   "kind": "fix",
   "text": "complaint:c_device: The listing has a Works with line naming the apps by device (iPad: Goodnotes, Notability, Noteshelf; Android: Samsung Notes, Xodo; Chromebook, Windows and Mac: Xodo or Adobe Acrobat Reader) and says it needs no Microsoft Word and no subscription. Landscape pages fit laptop screens as well as tablets. Start here step 1 repeats the app list."
  },
  {
   "key": "unique:u_money_month",
   "kind": "unique",
   "text": "Money month: A one-page money check for every month of 2027 plus Nov and Dec 2026, linked from each month page: money in by source and money out by cost type (planned and actual), totals and profit, orders or clients, best seller, what worked and one change for next month."
  },
  {
   "key": "unique:u_start_check",
   "kind": "unique",
   "text": "Start here, Setup check and a head start this week: A four-step Start here page (download in a browser, which app, pen off to tap, where to start for an Oct to Dec 2026 buyer and a 2027 buyer), a Setup check page whose buttons prove the links work, and Nov to Dec 2026 month and week pages starting Monday Oct 26, so a buyer can plan from the day they buy."
  },
  {
   "key": "unique:u_routines",
   "kind": "unique",
   "text": "Business routines and habit tracker: A Business routines checklist (every day, week, month and quarter: send orders, batch content, pay fees, put tax money aside, review prices) and a habit tracker page for every month, linked from the month page, for the business habits the owner picks (post daily, answer messages, log money)."
  },
  {
   "key": "unique:u_year_plan",
   "kind": "unique",
   "text": "Year plan with quarter ticks and Price check: A Year plan table (goal, why it matters, first step, a tick box for each quarter) and a Price check table (cost to make, fees and shipping, your time, price, profit each) for up to 18 products or services."
  },
  {
   "key": "look",
   "kind": "look",
   "text": "Quiet studio stationery: warm ivory paper (not white, so it glows less in a dark room) with charcoal ink at about 14:1 contrast so it stays sharp in daylight; secondary text in warm gray-brown at 6.4:1. The reviewer's two colors carry the palette: sand #C8B89A for the short ruled bar on the Contents and guide pages and as the first month tab, and warm taupe #7A7368 as the structure accent (habit circles, small graphics, never body text, since it is only 4.4:1 on the paper). Month tabs step from sand to a lighter taupe (#9C958B) so every tab label in charcoal stays above 5:1. Buttons are solid charcoal. Two font families only (r016): Libre Baskerville for headings and, in italic, for field labels; Jost for body, with bold for buttons and tabs. No letter-spaced all-caps labels (theme labels: italic). Plain ruled decoration (motif lines): no florals, no gold foil, no marble, no photos, no script fonts."
  }
 ],
